# Upstream sync before origin mainline push (HARD)

When committing/pushing a **mainline train** on a service repo (`mfi_integration_vX.Y.Z`, `mfi_release_vX.Y.Z`):

## Mandatory (every push)

1. `git fetch origin` and `git fetch upstream` **separately** (never one arg list for both).
2. Local branch tip must include **`upstream/<branch>` tip** (not behind).
3. If origin/local is behind upstream → say **STALE**, sync first (`bash scripts/bin/train-upstream-sync.sh --sync` or rebase onto `upstream/<branch>`), then push.
4. Push **origin only** via `bash scripts/bin/push-origin.sh` — never `upstream` / `trusttai`.
5. After sync, `git diff --name-only upstream/<branch>...HEAD` must contain **only** intended fix files (no unrelated noise).

## Machine gate

`scripts/bin/push-origin.sh` calls `train-upstream-sync.sh --check` (and `--sync` when tree is clean) before `git push` on train branches. Do not bypass with raw `git push` unless the user explicitly overrides.

## Why

Origin forks lag after trusttai merges. Pushing onto a stale origin tip creates a divergent mainline that is not the next-release line.

## Escape

`TRAIN_UPSTREAM_SYNC_SKIP=1` — rare; state aloud why. Prefer sync.

